{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>You hide</b> — the sense is, when You do not open Your hand, it is as though You have forgotten them or do not see them. Or: <i>they are dismayed</i>." "<b>You gather</b> — as though You say, by way of <i>'You gather to Yourself their spirit and their breath'</i> [cf. Psalm 104:29]." "<b>and to dust they return</b> — for the bones are in the living things of the earth, and in them."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 104, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:38:17.258784128Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}